            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Death and Memorials</strong><br>\nTubman died of pneumonia in 1913. Her life and work are commemorated through national parks, museums, and monuments across the United States.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Spiritual Life</strong><br>\nTubman's Christian faith was a driving force in her life. She believed her actions were guided by divine visions and dreams, giving her strength in her mission to free others.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Post-Civil War Activism</strong><br>\nAfter the abolition of slavery, Tubman continued to fight for equality and civil rights, supporting various causes to uplift the African American community and advance justice.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
